# Markdown documentation — U.S. English only

Every Markdown file under this repository (technical architecture
documents, runbooks, READMEs, functional specs, ADRs, release notes,
…) MUST be written in **American English**.

This rule applies whether you are creating a new document or editing
an existing one (including editing in place a section authored by
someone else). The only exception is verbatim third-party content
that we redistribute unchanged (e.g. `docs/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md`).

## Spelling — use the U.S. form

Do **not** use British / Commonwealth spellings. The most common
traps in this repo:

| Wrong (UK)              | Right (US)              |
|-------------------------|--------------------------|
| authorise / authorisation | authorize / authorization |
| behaviour                 | behavior                  |
| defence, defence-in-depth | defense, defense-in-depth |
| factorise / factorised    | factorize / factorized    |
| centralise / centralised  | centralize / centralized  |
| organise / organisation   | organize / organization   |
